        "original_paragraph": {
            "ITC Measurements": "Nano-ITC titrations were performed at 15 °C using a Nano-ITC instrument (TA Instruments, USA) equipped with a 300 μL active cell volume and a 50 μL stirring syringe. The protein sample was prepared in a buffer containing 20 mM Tris (pH 7.5), 300 mM NaCl, 0.01% 1-thioglycerol, and 10% glycerol. Titrations were carried out using an automated sequence of 25 injections of 2 μL of DD-1 solution (1 mM) or 20 injections of 2 μL of DD-2 solution into the sample cell containing PLK1 PBD solution (0.065 mM). Each injection was spaced at 200 s intervals to allow for complete equilibration. The Kd values of the DD-1 and DD-2 measured by Nano-ITC were 2.12 × 10^6 and 3.48 × 10^6 M−1, respectively."
        },
